==Enemy==
Surprisingly fast for a sloth, with speed somehow surpassing [[Elder Sloth]]. A weak [[Shield]] offers it a moment's protection, immunity to [[Wave Attack|Waves]] guards it from the likes of [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] and the default [[Cat Cannon]], and spikes from its tail hit three times and occasionally freeze Cats for a few seconds. Its multi-hits are fired in a rapid succession, with decreasing coverage that reaches up to 500px; the third hit has a range of 350~500, so units within that area will suffer the most damage unless knocked back.

==Strategy==
Most of the time, it acts as a backliner like its [[THE SLOTH|other]] [[Elder Sloth|variants]], but its Wave immunity makes it harder to snipe. Fortunately, its relatively slow attack rate and very weak Shield reduces the threat it poses. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is a great unit to use, as it can chip it down or outright destroy it if unprotected. Courier Cat is also able to tank two hits at a high enough level or a single hit from a 200% FOLIVOREAN. [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] can help with his Long Distance and Knockback against Aku threats, as well as being able to tank hits if his Tough Vs [[Talents|Talent]] has been unlocked. Most tanky low-ranged units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] still work, but only if this enemy is unprotected.

[[Ancient Egg: N006 (Special Cat)|Fallen Bear Cat]] is one of the most efficient attackers to use against THE FOLIVOREAN due to having both Behemoth Slayer and Insane Damage against Aku. It deals a whopping 119k damage against it initially and 189k at level 50. Starting at level 48, Fallen Bear Cat also has enough health to survive a hit from a 200% FOLIVOREAN.

With [https://youtu.be/tikfQbXjQ9k good timing] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]], rushers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] clip inside THE FOLIVOREAN's hitbox to attack it without further retaliation.

Above everything, do not let it reach your [[Cat Base]], as it can easily inflict extreme damage as soon as it gets within 500 range due to all of the damage being concentrated in an area 350-500 distance ahead of it.

