==Trivia==
*THE FOLIVOREAN's name is derived from ''[[wikipedia:Folivore|folivore]]'' (a herbivore that specializes in eating leaves, which sloths fall under) and ''[[wikipedia:Folivora|Folivora]]'' (the suborder of mammals commonly known as sloths).
*Its attack animation is a reference to ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Nargacuga|Nargacuga]], a Flying Wyvern that can eject spikes from its tail. Its blue fur resembles that of [[wikia:monsterhunter:Fiercewater Nargacuga|Fiercewater Nargacuga]] from the spin-off ''Monster Hunter Explore'', while its Freeze ability could be inspired by [[wikia:monsterhunter:Green Nargacuga|Green Nargacuga]], whose tail slam attacks Stun those hit.
**Its Japanese name, Namakemoruga (ナマケモルガ), is a portmanteau of ナマルケモルル ''Namarukemoruru'' ([[THE SLOTH]]'s Japanese name) and ''Nargacuga''.
*The phrase 最強の猛獣 ''saikyō no mōjū'' ("the strongest fierce beast") in THE FOLIVOREAN's Japanese description is also used in THE SLOTH's Japanese description and [[The Strongest Behemoth]]'s Japanese name. Although it was translated as "powerful Behemoth" and "Strongest Behemoth" in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], 猛獣 ''mōjū'' is different from the [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy type's Japanese name (超獣 ''Chōjū'', "Super-Beast").
*Its [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] type may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Diabolotherium|Diabolotherium]]'', an extinct genus of ground sloth whose name means "devil beast". Its Aku trait may also reference the [[wikipedia:Sloth (deadly sin)|sin of sloth]].

